Z||000000||L.I. Fieros||08-17-2001||07:10 PM||||Well, here's my newest problem.  I started my car up for the first time in about 2 months (been working on it) and now gas is pouring out from the fuel rail at the number 3 and 5 fuel injectors.  First I should let everyone know that the car was apart because I pulled the injectors and sent them out to have them rebuilt.  Was I supposed to do something special when I reinstalled the injectors into the fuel rail?  I got them back with new o-rings already on them.  Guess I am going to be re-doing the job tomorrow.  Is there anything I should know?  Or perhaps someone has seen this type of problem before?  Oh, and the motor was missing badly when I ran it.  So, I'm guessing the number 3 and/or 5 cylinders are not getting any fuel.  The injectors not firing shouldn't cause fuel to pour out though.  However, fuel leaking out could cause the miss.  Oh well.<P>Hope this is all worth it...<BR>Thanks,<BR>Dave<BR>Long Island Fiero Enthusiasts||||reg||9
